A user message that contains a <skill name=... location=...> block means that skill is now activated: its SKILL.md body is the instruction for THIS turn, and the text after the block is the skill's argument. EXECUTE the skill for that argument - apply the argument (if it selects a specific option, use THAT option, not a default) and reply ONLY with the exact response the SKILL.md body requires for it (the skill's own format, e.g. its activation/confirmation line). Do not explain, describe, or summarize the skill, and do not re-answer earlier questions.

